WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:14.150
On a Monday night in September 2015, in a little town outside New Delhi,

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:17.940
an angry mob showed up to the house of man named Mohammad Akhlaq.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:35.260
The mob hit Akhlaq's elderly mother. They severely injured his son and then, they found Akhlaq.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.920
They dragged him on to the street and they
beat him with bricks until he immediately died.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.860
The reason Akhlaq was killed, the anger from
this mob

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.980
came from a rumor, a rumor that he was
carrying beef.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:59.520
"56 year old Muslim man was beaten to death
by an allegedly Hindu mob."

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.980
An investigation was immediately launched.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:08.640
Not only into Akhlaq's murder, but also into whether or not he truly was carrying beef.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.340
18 suspects were identified, but now, four
years later,

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.280
the trial hasn't even begun yet. In fact,
the accused are out on bail,

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.320
which has led to fear among the victim's
family and community.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:34.780
Earlier this year, one of the accused was invited to sit in the front row of a political rally.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.610
He later claimed that 16 of the accused
were in the audience that day.

00:01:39.610 --> 00:01:42.780
Aklhaq's murder isn't an isolated incident.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.960
Here in a town in eastern India, two Muslim

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:49.860
cattle traders, one of them 
 just 13, we're driving to a fair to

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.689
sell their cows when they were stopped
by a group of men, who beat them and hanged

00:01:54.689 --> 00:01:59.869
them from a tree where, they both died.
Over the last seven years hundreds of

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:04.979
Indians have been attacked, many killed.
This violence has affected some Hindus

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.900
and other minorities, but the majority of the
victims are Muslims.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:15.500
All these incidents plotted on the map have one thing
in common: they're all directly tied to cows.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.600
But these attacks like this weren't always this
prevalent.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.200
In 2012, there was just one such attack in
all of India.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.240
The next year there were just two.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.880
But then in 2014, something changed.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.860
Look at the rise every year since.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.780
And if you look closer at what's actually happening

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:49.660
on the ground, you can start to see exactly why
these violent attacks are on the rise.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:55.160
"Showing violence by so-called cow
vigilantes in India."

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:00.410
"Self-appointed guardians of cows, which
are sacred to Hindus claim they're being

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.700
illegally slaughtered. Not afraid to use
violence to stop them."

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.780
There are millions of stray cows in India.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.500
These cows don't belong to anyone.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.440
They are usually past the age where they
can be productive on farms and so

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.480
they're just set free to roam the
country and you see them everywhere.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:39.560
Cows are considered sacred in Hinduism and the majority of India's 1.3 billion people identify as Hindu.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:56.840
Cows are generally revered by Hindus, many
of whom abstain from eating beef,

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:01.320
but many Indians practice religions
that don't share that same belief.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.880
While transporting and trading cows isn't
always illegal in the country,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:10.470
slaughtering cows is banned in most of
India's states. In some parts of the

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:14.570
country, especially those in the northern
region, the police go on raids looking

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:19.709
for people who are breaking these cow
protection laws, but in recent years,

00:04:19.709 --> 00:04:21.580
it's not just the police cracking down.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:25.550
These are cow vigilantes.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:31.100
"Once again, the beef brigade has taken law
in its own hands in this country."

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:38.040
"This is one of several viral video showing
violence by so-called cow vigilantes in India."

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.850
"A resident of Haryana's Mewat district was
transporting two cows in

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:44.160
his vehicle when he was beaten to
death."

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:50.340
They're almost always groups of young men
piling into SUVs to patrol the highways at night.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:57.120
They'll take whatever weapons they have. Rifles or like small handmade guns. Then, they'll raid the highways

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:03.000
looking for any vehicle. Sometimes
they'll have police around with them.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.130
Sometimes they will be on the phone with
the police. That's Snigdha Poonam.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:10.250
She's a national affairs writer with The
Hindustan Times in Delhi.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.810
And I've been one of these vehicles with them
for a

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:15.150
midnight raid and everyone has to stop,

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:20.620
even if it's like a group of young
people driving late at night, they have

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:26.160
to stop and these cow protectors can do with
them as they please.

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:29.540
If these vigilantes hear about someone

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:33.250
who's in possession of a cow or is
carrying beef, sometimes they will turn

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:38.460
them over to the police, but more and
more, they've been using violence on their own.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:48.080
Often they make videos and then, that starts
passing around on Facebook and Whatsapp.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:57.880
Many cow vigilante's have ties with
Hindu militant groups that specifically

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:03.890
target Muslims and other religious minorities.
According to a Human Rights Watch report,

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:10.680
between 2015 and 2018, of the 44 cow-related deaths, 36 of them were Muslim.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.360
To understand why these attacks
have surged during this time you have to

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.920
look at the rise of one of India's
biggest political parties.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.360
"It's interesting to take a look at why and how this has become

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:30.520
such a massive landslide in terms of seats
has been unprecedented. 70 seats for the BJP."

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:37.430
In 2014, India's Hindu nationalist party
called Bharatiya Janata Party or BJP won

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:43.320
the national elections and that made the leader
of the party, Narendra Modi, the Prime minister of India.

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.940
His political platform has long been this
idea of

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:54.080
Hindu nationalism and a big focus of
his speeches has been the protection of cows.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.540
One of the things that Narendra
Modi did while campaigning was talk

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:14.900
about cows and how cows needed to be
saved or worshipped or celebrated.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.520
Let's look at this map again, which shows
how cow violence increased after 2014,

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:28.280
but now look at the attacks of 2017 and
2018. You can see that most of them are

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:33.380
clustered around this one area. This is
Uttar Pradesh or UP.

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:37.110
With over 200 million people, this is India's
most populous state

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:44.500
and in 2017, the Modi government appointed
this man to be the leader of the state, Yogi Adityanath.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:50.780
Earlier this year at an election rally,
Yogi referred to Muslims as quote a

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:55.710
"green virus." In fact, it was at one of his
political rallies where one of Akhlaq's

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:59.040
accused murderers was invited to sit on
the front row.

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.040
After being appointed, Yogi directed the
police to scrutinize the slaughterhouses

00:08:25.050 --> 00:08:29.260
in his state, shutting down any that
didn't have the proper paperwork.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:33.519
They shuttered thousands of meat shops and
closed hundreds of slaughterhouses that

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:38.580
they claimed were illegal putting many
Muslims in Uttar Pradesh out of business.

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:43.140
And with Yogi in power, cow vigilantes were
quickly emboldened.

00:08:43.150 --> 00:08:48.200
In fact soon after he was appointed, three
meat shops were set on fire by a mob.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.660
That year cow related violence spiked in UP

00:08:51.860 --> 00:08:54.620
and the impact of the Yogi's policies didn't
end there.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:07.860
I traveled south from the capital of UP, where
Yogi's office sits, to a city on the banks of the Ganges.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.440
I'm in a part of Uttar Pradesh, which is
a huge leather producer and just a few

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:24.600
months ago the government gave a notice to
this factory that they needed to stop all operations.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:31.560
They used water pollution
as the excuse because leather production

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:37.150
uses water and can pollute rivers and things
like that so this factory worked really

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:42.731
hard to install pumps and filters and
even after they provided all of the

00:09:42.731 --> 00:09:46.630
information and jumped through all those
hoops, the government still hasn't given

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:53.120
them permission to open up the factory again
and so it's sits completely shut down, frozen in time.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:18.000
All of these workers, the owners, everyone
here is Muslim and this has been an

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:22.560
industry that Muslims in Uttar Pradesh
have worked in for many many years

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.860
and it's now completely halted.

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:52.400
I'm associated with the industry for
the last 50 years. I have never seen such bad days.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.880
Since he came into power in
2017, Yogi has allocated government

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:08.670
funding to build shelters for stray cows
around his state. I went to visit one of

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:13.030
these shelters to meet with the head of
a local cow protection organization.

00:11:13.030 --> 00:11:16.830
As someone who has dedicated his life to
peaceful and lawful cow protection,

00:11:16.830 --> 00:11:21.840
he was excited when Yogi announced his plan
to construct many more cow shelters.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:41.960
The place is not actually protecting or
supporting cows. It's a lot that exists here

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:46.800
for the cows to be in, but these
cows are starving, you can see their ribs.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:49.680
They don't have enough food. They don't
have enough shade.

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:59.710
The state government has used the setting
up of a lot of

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:01.690
these cow shelters as a political

00:12:01.690 --> 00:12:07.450
showcase of their commitment to Hindu
ideals, but when you come look at them

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:13.320
you realize this isn't about protecting
cows. This is about fueling an ideology.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:17.940
Akhlaq was killed by a mob because of
a rumor that he had beef in his

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:22.840
possession, but the murder investigation
revealed that the meat he was carrying was not beef.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:24.560
It was mutton.

00:12:25.060 --> 00:12:30.140
Akhlaq's brothers suspect that the murder
has less to do with cows and beef

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.520
and more to do with the fact that he was a
Muslim who had money.

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:41.400
It's not about cows. It's how they feel that
the Muslims have risen.

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:46.840
They are buying more land. They are buying
better houses

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:53.020
or they are earning more. They are rising
and how that upsets their social position.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:13:00.480
After a series of horrific cow related incidents
in 2017,

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:04.730
thousands took to the street in protest
prompting Prime minister Modi to break

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:08.480
his silence and finally condemn violence
in the name of cows.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:21.600
Then, in 2018, the Indian Supreme Court passed
a series of directives urging state governments

00:13:21.600 --> 00:13:26.880
to take the problem more seriously, to
properly prosecute these cases.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:30.520
Some state governments have tried to raise
awareness to curb the rumors that incite

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:35.440
this violence, but no official action has
been taken by the national government.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:42.000
Meanwhile, Modi just won another
nationwide election and Yogi remains in power.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:48.260
And India, this country that is
rooted in the ideals of secularism and diversity

00:13:48.440 --> 00:13:53.300
has become more and more
dangerous for millions of its Muslim citizens.

